      {
        "id": 95255,
        "name": "Edwin",
        "username": "Edwin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/73ab20/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-01T22:22:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Foote wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Humble-Knight wrote:<br><blockquote>But I do think that means the Sentinels deal +1 damage to one another&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nyup\n</blockquote></div>\nexactly\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This would make more sense if they weren't all such a happy family…they're an homage to Fantastic Four, and you know that Ben and Johnny are dealing extra damage to each other, as are Sue and Reed (at least with psychic damage), and for that matter Sue and Johnny since they're siblings.&nbsp; But I don't get a vibe like that from the Sentinels at all.</p>\n<p>Still, it means Hippocratic Oath makes Medico a <em>great</em> healer for the rest of his team.&nbsp; Do a Coordinated Assault on the Idealist and you're giving her back more than half her starting HP, assuming Writhe and Mainstay are both still up.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:02.901Z",
