        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I get the line that Ronway listed but thematically I would think based on how The Sentinels work that they aren't considered to be a nemesis of each other. &nbsp;I would make an exception of it for the Sentinels or just not play with the nemesis rule. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well the Ennead members arn't \"nemmys\" of eachother, but because they are a \"team\", any backstabbing (accidental or otherwise) hurts that much more. Thematically it can work any way you want it to work. Playing with the nemesis rule isn't a nessesity to the gameplay at all. You could ignore the nemmy rule in all your games and still have a good time.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:22:03.221Z",
